      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In-stent restenosis represents a pathological process which histology is different from that of restenosis after balloon angioplasty. In-stent restenosis is mainly caused by neointima proliferation. This part of review deals with technologies of prevention of in-stent restenosis including novel stent designs and coatings aimed at suppression of neointima proliferation."},
